From bec6554037f304c300ff9beae2a4aeef10dbec34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Allow an experience to belong to multiple macrocategories
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 6 categories (Sea/Gourmet/Wine/Wild/Wellness/Cultural Escape) were a single-select field per experience, driving the configurator's matching directly. Added experience_content.categories (text[]), backfilled from the old single category column (kept, unused by app code going forward, no destructive migration). Admin Filters card: category dropdown -> checkbox grid, same pattern already used for guests/budget/time-slot filters. Updated every place that compared categories by equality to use array overlap instead: generateProposal.ts's category match / best-experience pick / add-ons exclusion, buildRendererData.ts's included-experiences candidate pool, plus the admin list search/badges and a few cosmetic display spots. Verified the new matching logic against 5 scenarios (multi-category match, best-experience pick when the matching category isn't first in the array, partial-overlap exclusion) with an isolated test — all pass. /submit-experience (partner intake form) intentionally left single-select: it never writes to experience_content, admins categorize the real experience manually after reviewing a submission.
